# React + TypeScript

- Use functional components and typed props. Prefer named exports for components/hooks; default export is fine for route `App` entry.
- Colocate route screens under `src/pages/` and shared pieces under `src/components/`.
- Style with Tailwind utility classes; avoid new CSS modules or inline style objects unless necessary.
- Do not add `useMemo` / `useCallback` by default — only when there is a measured need or an existing pattern.
- Prefer `import type` for type-only imports (`verbatimModuleSyntax` is on).
- Match Prettier (single quotes, no semicolons, trailing commas) and existing file structure.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
import type { ReactNode } from 'react'
import { isSupabaseConfigured } from '@/lib/supabase'

export function StatusBadge({ label }: { label: string }) {
  return <span className="text-sm text-slate-600">{label}</span>
}
```
